hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16768","He said: al-Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah, and I heard it myself from al-Haytham, he said: Hafs ibn Maysara narrated to us, from Ibn Harmala, from Abu Thifal al-Murri, that he said: I heard Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Huwaytib say: my grandmother narrated to me that she heard her father say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no prayer for one without wudu, and no wudu for one who does not mention Allah, exalted, and does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and does not believe in me who does not love the Ansar."
"16769","He said: Shayban narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abu Thifal, with this hadith, and he said: She heard her father Said ibn Zayd."
